			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose RPC modules into file-per-struct submodules\n\nRefactor all `Source/RPC/*.rs` files to align with the project-wide PascalCase module path convention enforced in recent `Track` and `RunTime` refactors. Replace inline struct definitions and `pub use` re-exports with explicit `pub mod` declarations that delegate to sibling files (e.g., `CommandService.rs`, `EchoActionServer.rs`).\n\nThis change ensures that every struct and implementation resides in a file matching its PascalCase name, allowing Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro to correctly resolve `__cmd__` symbols via the full module path. Placeholder services (Debug, Processes, SCM, Terminals, Windows) are updated to use the `Struct` naming pattern within their feature gates, while active services (Commands, Configuration, EchoAction, Telemetry, Workspace, Types, Vine) are split into their constituent DTOs and service handles. The `EchoAction` module retains its complex logic but now delegates to dedicated sub-files for `EchoActionServer`, `ExtensionHostRegistry`, `ExtensionRouter`, and priority resolution.\n\nThis establishes a consistent architectural pattern across the entire RPC layer, eliminating flat imports and ensuring strict path resolution for IPC generation.",
