				940,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Enforce PascalCase paths in Effect module tree\n\nUpdate the `Track::Effect` module to align with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention and strict path resolution required by Tauri's command macros.\n\nIn `CreateEffectForRequest/mod.rs`, rename the exported function from `CreateEffectForRequest` to `Fn` to match the import pattern used in `DispatchFrontendCommand` and other callers. In `mod.rs`, remove legacy `pub use` re-exports and the `pub mod` exposure pattern that allowed flat imports. Replace them with an explicit `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` directive and documentation comments.\n\nThis enforces that callers must spell out the full double-segment paths (e.g., `Track::Effect::CreateEffectForRequest::Fn`). This structure is mandatory for `tauri::generate_handler!` to correctly locate the `__cmd__` companion symbols while maintaining PascalCase file and module names, ensuring consistency across the Mountain crate and resolving potential symbol resolution issues in the IPC layer.\n\nAdditionally, format function signatures in `Keybinding.rs` and `NativeHost.rs` to single lines and expand comments in `Webview.rs` for clarity.",
